7592186444274 13194139534923 17592186045417 true] [17592186444324 1075 #edb/ref 17592186444294 13194139534923 17592186045417 true] [17592186444324 1075 #edb/ref 17592186444295 13194139534923 17592186045417 true] [17592186444324 1075 #edb/ref 17592186444305 13194139534923 17592186045417 true] [17592186444324 1075 #edb/ref 17592186444314 13194139534923 17592186045417 true] [17592186444324 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534923 17592186045417 true] [17592186444324 1077 "selection" 13194139534923 17592186045417 true] [17592186444324 1078 #edb/ref 17592186444295 13194139534923 17592186045417 true] [17592186444324 1079 #uuid "d4649305-d5dc-5854-97b6-ea90ae323c38" 13194139534923 17592186045417 true] [17592186444325 1068 #edb/ref 17592186444321 13194139534923 17592186045417 true] [17592186444325 1069 "q-132071" 13194139534923 17592186045417 true] [17592186444325 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534923 17592186045417 true] [17592186444325 1071 "Using the cross product curvature formula, find the curvature of $r(t)=⟨t,\\,\\sqrt{t}⟩$ as a function of $t.$" 13194139534923 17592186045417 true] [17592186444325 1072 #uuid "076128a8-7495-5bb6-b7b4-2c35cb671771" 13194139534923 17592186045417 true] [17592186444325 1074 "The curvature $κ$ is given by\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(t),\\,\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\sqrt{t})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}}⟩ \\\\ ‖{r}^{′}(t)‖ & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{(\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+\\frac{1}{4t}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{4t+1}{4t}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{4t+1}}{2\\sqrt{t}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the second derivative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{″}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(1),\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,-\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{{t}^{3}}}⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we compute the cross product by considering ${r}^{′}(t)$ and ${r}^{″}(t)$ as $3$-dimensional vectors with zero $z$-components:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t) & =⟨1,\\,\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}},\\,0⟩\\times ⟨0,\\,-\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{{t}^{3}}},\\,0⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}} & 0 \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{{t}^{3}}} & 0\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}1 & \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{t}} &  \\\\ 0 & -\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{{t}^{3}}}\\end{aligned}\\right|\\,k \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{{t}^{3}}}\\,k\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the magnitude of the cross product is\n\n$$\n‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖=\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{{t}^{3}}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}κ(t) & =\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{{t}^{3}}})}{{(\\frac{\\sqrt{4t+1}}{2\\sqrt{t}})}^{3}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{1}{4\\sqrt{{t}^{3}}})}{(\\frac{\\sqrt{(4t+1)^{3}}}{8\\sqrt{{t}^{3}}})} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{(4t+1)^{3}}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534923 17592186045417 true] [17592186444326 1068 #edb/ref 17592186444322 13194139534923 17592186045417 true] [17592186444326 1069 "q-165246" 13194139534923 17592186045417 true] [17592186444326 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139534923 17592186045417 true] [17592186444326 1071 "Given the curve $r(t)=⟨6t,\\,{t}^{3},\\,3{t}^{2}⟩,$ use the cross product curvature formula to find the curvature of this curve as a function of $t.$ \n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that* ${r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)=18(-{t}^{2}\\,i-2\\,j+2t\\,k).$" 13194139534923 17592186045417 true] [17592186444326 1072 #uuid "0b5962d7-05b0-532b-8c6d-f094e8fba0fc" 13194139534923 17592186045417 true] [17592186444326 1074 "The curvature $κ(t)$ is given by\n\n$$\nκ(t)=\\frac{‖{r}^{′}(t)\\times {r}^{″}(t)‖}{‖{r}^{′}(t){‖}^{3}}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we calculate ${r}^{′}(t)$ and $‖{r}^{′}(t)‖:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}^{′}(t) & =⟨\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}t}(6t),\\,\\frac{\\text{